.TH DIFFA 1 "November 2025" "diffa 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffa \- snapshot, compare, patch, and sync directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffa
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffa
is a command-line tool for file system comparison, patching, and synchronization on macOS and Linux. It provides snapshot-based directory comparison, patch creation/application, and folder synchronization with conflict resolution.
.PP
The tool uses SQLite-based storage for efficient handling of large directory structures (100k+ files) with minimal memory usage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B snapshot
Create a snapshot of a directory
.TP
.B compare
Compare two directories or snapshots
.TP
.B patch
Create, apply, or revert patches (subcommands: create, apply, revert)
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize two directories (unidirectional or bidirectional)
.TP
.B export
Export patch in various formats
.TP
.B verify
Verify a directory matches a snapshot
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help information
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a snapshot of a directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa snapshot /path/to/dir \-o snapshot.diffa
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compare two directories:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa compare /dir\-a /dir\-b
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create and apply a patch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa patch create /old /new \-o update.patch
diffa patch apply update.patch /target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Synchronize directories:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa sync /source /dest
diffa sync /dir\-a /dir\-b \-\-bidirectional
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify directory integrity:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa verify /path/to/dir baseline.diffa
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or no differences for compare/verify)
.TP
.B 1
Differences found (compare/verify) or operational errors
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid arguments)
.TP
.B 3
File system error (permission denied, not found, etc.)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.diffa
Snapshot files (SQLite databases)
.TP
.I *.patch
Patch files (SQLite databases)
.TP
.I ~/.cache/diffa/
Cache directory for large file content (patches with files ≥1MB)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffa\-snapshot (1),
.BR diffa\-compare (1),
.BR diffa\-patch (1),
.BR diffa\-sync (1),
.BR diffa\-export (1),
.BR diffa\-verify (1),
.BR rsync (1)
